            <ArticleTitle>Bigeminal and trigeminal distribution of ventricular extrasystoles as an expression of &quot;atypical&quot; concealed bigeminy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>758-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report reflects a case of bigeminal and trigeminal ventricular extrasystoles where bigeminal extrasystoles are associated with short coupling intervals, while trigeminal extrasystoles manifest long coupling intervals. The arrhythmia is interpreted as an &quot;atypical&quot; form of concealed bigeminy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
